	Interview answer
    Thread priority is a value assigned to a thread that indicates its relative importance to the scheduler. Java supports priorities from 1 to 10, with 5 as the default. However, thread priority is only a scheduling hint and does not guarantee execution order.

18. yield()
    yield() is a static method of the Thread class. It gives a hint to the thread scheduler that the current thread is willing to temporarily give up the CPU so that other threads of the same or higher priority may get a chance to execute.

	⭐ Interview answer
    Thread.yield() is a static method that gives a hint to the thread scheduler that the current thread is willing to temporarily yield the CPU, allowing other eligible threads to get a chance to execute. However, the scheduler is free to ignore this request.
    Easy memory:
