   Thread.sleep() is used to pause the execution of the current thread for a specified period. After that period, the thread becomes eligible for execution again. sleep() does not release any lock held by the thread.
   class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws InterruptedException {

        System.out.println("Start");

        Thread.sleep(3000);  // 3 seconds

        System.out.println("End");
    }
  }
  ⭐Remember
