38. what is dead lock and how can we avoid this?
    Deadlock is a situation where two or more threads are permanently blocked because each thread is holding a lock and waiting for another lock held by another thread.
	Thread 1                  Thread 2
   |                         |
   | acquires Lock A         | acquires Lock B
   ↓                         ↓
 waits for Lock B          waits for Lock A
   |                         |
   └───────── waits ─────────┘
   ⭐⭐⭐
   How can we avoid deadlock?
   a. Always acquire locks in the same order
   b. Avoid unnecessary nested locks
   c. Use tryLock() with a timeout
   Consistent lock ordering + minimize nested locks + use timed tryLock() when appropriate.

