46. what is Executor framewok?
    Executor Framework is a framework provided in the java.util.concurrent package that helps manage and execute threads. It separates task submission from thread creation and thread management, typically using thread pools.

	Without Executor Framework:
    Thread t1 = new Thread(task1);
    Thread t2 = new Thread(task2);
	t1.start();
    t2.start();

	with executor framework
	ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(2);
     executor.submit(task1);
     executor.submit(task2);

	 executor.shutdown();

47. Why Executor Framework?
    We use the Executor Framework to separate task submission from thread management. It provides thread pools, which allow us to reuse threads, reduce the overhead of creating new threads, control the number of concurrent threads, and efficiently execute multiple tasks.

