56. How ThreadPoolExecutor works
    ThreadPoolExecutor maintains a pool of worker threads. When we submit a task, the executor places it in a work queue if a worker thread is not immediately available. Worker threads continuously take tasks from the queue and execute them. After completing one task, the worker thread can be reused for another task.

57.	Core pool size, Maximum pool size
    Core pool size = the minimum number of worker threads that the pool tries to keep available.
	Maximum pool size = the maximum number of worker threads that the executor can create.

