63. StampedLock
    StampedLock is another locking mechanism introduced in Java 8.
    It supports three modes:

    a)Read lock
	long stamp = lock.readLock();

    try {
    // read data
    } finally {
    lock.unlockRead(stamp);
    }


    b)Write lock
	long stamp = lock.writeLock();

    try {
    // modify data
    } finally {
    lock.unlockWrite(stamp);
    }

    c)Optimistic read	:-"I'll read the data without acquiring a traditional read lock. After reading, I'll check whether a writer changed the data."

	long stamp = lock.tryOptimisticRead();
     int value = data;

     if (!lock.validate(stamp)) {
    stamp = lock.readLock();
    try {
        value = data;
    } finally {
        lock.unlockRead(stamp);
    }
   }

