How to choose pool size?
For CPU-bound tasks, a pool size close to the number of available CPU cores is a good starting point. For I/O-bound tasks, we can use a larger pool because threads spend time waiting for I/O. A common starting formula is cores × (1 + wait time / compute time), but the final value should be determined through monitoring and load testing.






